From: SamuriHL <samurihl@msn.com>
Subject: tdm: use consumer IEC60958 channel status for multi-channel LPCM

Multi-channel LPCM hardcoded its IEC60958 channel status (0x15/0x55/0xfa/
0x32) instead of using the computed one. Byte 0 bit 0 is the professional/
consumer flag, so every 5.1/7.1 PCM stream declared IEC60958 PROFESSIONAL
mode over a consumer HDMI link; byte 2 carried channel 0xf / source 0xa.

The L-PCM audio InfoFrame sets coding type 0, "refer to stream header",
which points the sink at the channel status. An AVR that honours it
declines to decode the stream as consumer multi-channel and falls back to
stereo - even though the InfoFrame itself is correct. Verified on an Ugoos
AM9 Pro (S6): CC=6, CA=0x0B, AUD_MODE=0x70, I2S_IN_MAP=0x24,
AUDP_TXCTRL=0x02 and TDMOUT-B lane masks all 0x3, yet the AVR reported 2.0.

Confirmed by writing the registers on a live 6-channel stream, in both
directions and with a no-op control:

  fresh stream, hardcoded 0x15/0x55/0xfa/0x32 -> AVR 2.0
  no-op write (0x15 -> 0x15)                  -> AVR 2.0
  write 0x00/0x01/0x10/0x02                   -> AVR 5.1
  repeat of the above                         -> AVR 5.1
  fresh stream, driver rewrites hardcoded     -> AVR 2.0

Which of the four bytes the sink objects to was not isolated; the change
restores all of them to the values the consumer PCM path already produces.

The status cannot be computed from the stream's own codec type:
codec_is_raw() counts AUD_CODEC_TYPE_MULTI_LPCM as raw, so
iec_get_channel_status_info() returns compressed-audio status with
IEC958_AES0_NONAUDIO set, which mutes the stream outright. Compute it as
AUD_CODEC_TYPE_STEREO_PCM instead - the consumer PCM branch, which yields
0x00/0x01/0x10/0x02 at 48kHz and, unlike the raw branch, is also correct at
88.2/96/176.4/192kHz and derives word length from the sample depth.
codec_type itself is left intact for the channel mask and event type.

Confined to the I2S->HDMITX path on hdmitx21: set_aud_param_ch_status() is
static with one call site, SPDIF and eARC compute their own status, and
hdmitx20 never reads aud_param->status[] (so this is a no-op on G12B).

--- a/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/tdm.c	2026-08-05 18:22:52.916525262 -0400
+++ b/sound/soc/amlogic/auge/tdm.c	2026-08-05 18:37:00.249919934 -0400
@@ -1811,12 +1811,6 @@
 	struct aud_para *aud_param, enum aud_codec_types codec_type)
 {
 	switch (codec_type) {
-		case AUD_CODEC_TYPE_MULTI_LPCM:
-			aud_param->status[0] = 0x15;
-			aud_param->status[1] = 0x55;
-			aud_param->status[2] = 0xfa;
-			aud_param->status[3] = 0x32;
-			break;
 		default:
 			aud_param->status[0] = chsts->chstat0_l & 0xff;
 			aud_param->status[1] = (chsts->chstat0_l >> 8) & 0xff;
@@ -2013,6 +2007,7 @@
 		/* i2s source to hdmix */
 		if (get_hdmitx_audio_src(rtd->card) > HDMITX_SRC_SPDIF) {
 			enum aud_codec_types codec_type = get_i2s2hdmitx_audio_format(rtd->card);
+			enum aud_codec_types cs_codec_type;
 			int i2s_out_data_lane_mask = get_hdmitx_i2s_mask(rtd->card);
 			unsigned int event_type = 0;
 			struct iec958_chsts chsts;
@@ -2067,7 +2062,18 @@
 				event_type = AOUT_EVENT_RAWDATA_DTS_HD_MA;
 			else
 				event_type = AOUT_EVENT_IEC_60958_PCM;
-			iec_get_channel_status_info(&chsts, codec_type,
+			/* Multi-channel LPCM is consumer PCM, but codec_is_raw()
+			 * counts it as raw, so computing the channel status with its
+			 * own codec type returns compressed-audio status (NONAUDIO
+			 * set, category DVD) and the sink mutes the stream. Compute
+			 * it as stereo PCM - the consumer PCM path, which also gets
+			 * every sample rate and the word length right - while leaving
+			 * codec_type itself intact for the channel mask and event
+			 * type above.
+			 */
+			cs_codec_type = (codec_type == AUD_CODEC_TYPE_MULTI_LPCM) ?
+				AUD_CODEC_TYPE_STEREO_PCM : codec_type;
+			iec_get_channel_status_info(&chsts, cs_codec_type,
 				runtime->rate, bit_depth, 0);
 			set_aud_param_ch_status(&chsts, &aud_param, codec_type);
 			aout_notifier_call_chain(event_type, &aud_param);
